## sym.rel — relationships declared, not discovered

The newest band generalizes "ODE law on a generator" to *declared relationships in general*. A `rel:v1` registry names generators and attaches derivative laws in a second phase — `rel-seed` declares the name, `rel-law` attaches `D(g)` as an expression over x and other generators, so cyclic pairs resolve:

```koru
import std/io
import std/sym

// condensed from 615_049: cyclic laws, then the conservation check.
std/sym:rel-new(): r0
|> std/sym:rel-seed(reg: r0, name: "sin")
    | exact r1 |> std/sym:rel-seed(reg: r1, name: "cos")
        | exact r2 |> std/sym:rel-law(reg: r2, name: "sin", law: "g(cos)")
            | exact r3 |> std/sym:rel-law(reg: r3, name: "cos", law: "(-1e0*g(sin))")
                | exact r4 |> std/sym:rel-derive(reg: r4, a: "g(sin)*g(sin)+g(cos)*g(cos)")
                    | exact d |> std/io:print.ln("{{ d:s }}") |> std/io:free(content: d)
                        |> std/io:free(content: r4)
                    | unknown-generator |> std/io:print.ln("unknown-generator") |> std/io:free(content: r4)
                    | lawless |> std/io:print.ln("lawless") |> std/io:free(content: r4)
                    | bad |> std/io:print.ln("bad") |> std/io:free(content: r4)
                | unknown-generator |> std/io:print.ln("unknown-generator")
                | bad |> std/io:print.ln("bad")
            | unknown-generator |> std/io:print.ln("unknown-generator")
            | bad |> std/io:print.ln("bad")
        | dup |> std/io:print.ln("dup")
        | full |> std/io:print.ln("full")
        | bad |> std/io:print.ln("bad")
    | dup |> std/io:print.ln("dup")
    | full |> std/io:print.ln("full")
    | bad |> std/io:print.ln("bad")
```

`rel-derive` prints `0e0` — the conservation of `sin² + cos²` proven mechanically, since every rewrite step is a derivative rule or a declared-law substitution. `rel-norm` canonicalizes for caller-side equality checks. Generator references form their own expression universe — `g(name)` parses only under a registry, so `<sexpr!>` values can't leak in and rel text can't leak out into `sym:add`; undeclared names refuse `unknown-generator`, deriving a lawless generator refuses `lawless`.

